    "raw": "Build an unsupervised pipeline (not IDF/BM25, not supervised ST fine-tuning) that reads our documents and todo text, embeds chunks with sentence-transformers (or compatible dense embedder), and derives terms/phrases that are semantically important in vector space for our domain.\n\nContext from design discussion:\n- Hash embedder and lexical boosts are insufficient for semantic vocabulary discovery.\n- sentence-transformers encode() is the engine only; importance scoring is our pipeline.\n- NOT Apple Create ML / NLContextualEmbedding.\n- NOT document-frequency IDF scores; importance means discriminative/salient in embedding geometry (e.g. term vectors aligned with doc/cluster centroids and far from global corpus centroid; KeyBERT-style doc-term cosine; cluster representatives after UMAP/HDBSCAN).\n\nRelates to todo-embedding branch (sqlite + search) but this ticket is the separate semantic vocabulary layer: corpus ingest, candidate phrase mining, embed, score, persist term table, expose via todo.py (e.g. terms list / terms for doc / search boost hook).\n\nStart after or alongside merging todo-embedding sqlite storage.\n\n--- Curated tags -> embedding phrases (concept; NOT fleshed out here) ---\nA curated tag names a bucket that expands to a list of embedding phrases, e.g.\n  code-health -> [\"test\", \"pytest\", \"iamlazy test\", \"playwright mcp\", ...]\nAuto-tagging matches a todo against these phrase lists (cosine) to assign tags.\nEmpirical note: an unspecialized general embedder (Apple NLCE) does NOT cleanly\nrank such phrases -- compressed cosine range, keys on shared surface tokens over\nconcept (e.g. \"technical debt\" / \"software quality\" score BELOW distractors vs a\n\"code health\" anchor). Motivates the domain-tuned importance pipeline above, not\na raw general embedder. Stop here for now.\n\n--- Planned subtodo (subtask of this ticket): manual `todo tag` mechanism ---\nSeeds the tag corpus, which starts EMPTY. Implementing agent wires the spawn +\nwait-and-merge workitems; NOT spawned here.\n`todo tag <id> <tag>*`:\n- Manually add one or more tags to a todo. Additive; manual tags are NEVER\n  auto-deleted.\n- Tags surfaced in display: shown in `ls` and `search` output.\n- Tags found by search: auto AND manual tags are embedded and become a THIRD\n  cosine match target (alongside the Summary and Body vectors).\n- Out of scope (later): grooming/bucketing tags and deriving the curated\n  tag -> phrase lists that auto-tag todos.\n- Manual tags are retained as regression backstops for the next tagging-training\n  phase.\n\n--- Groom note (2026-07-29) ---\nThe planned manual `todo tag` subtodo above has SHIPPED separately: 5da67f94\n(persisted explicit tags) then ee1799aa (plural provenance-tracked Tag field\n{raw, manual, vectors}; tagadd/tagrm; doctor-recomputed AUTOMATIC zero-shot\ntags from Summary+Body; schema v7; tags rank in search; -g column). Do not\nre-plan it here. Remaining scope of THIS ticket is the domain-tuned\nimportance pipeline (corpus ingest, candidate mining, embed, score, persist\nterm table, todo.py surface) plus, later, the curated tag -> phrase-bucket\nexpansion sketched above. ef4ad78d's noted future work (hubness correction,\nlinguistic pruning) belongs here too.\n\n--- GROOMED DESIGN (2026-07-29) -- read this before coding ---\n\nCode recon findings (what ALREADY exists -- do not rebuild):\n- ST embedder: todo_embed.py SentenceTransformerEmbedder (all-MiniLM-L6-v2,\n  normalize_embeddings=True) is registered as key \"st\" in _BACKENDS (hidden,\n  opt-in, lazy import). The AC's \"dense embedder\" item is DONE; select it with\n  --embedder=st. Do not add a new embedder.\n- Vector plumbing: TodoStore (todo_store.py) persists per-field chunk vectors\n  on BOTH backends (inline in ticket JSON; sqlite adds a derived embeddings\n  index -- see has_vector_index). all_embeddings/put_embedding/\n  embeddings_for_ticket are the API. search_tickets backfills missing vectors\n  for non-cheap embedders at search time (\"refreshing embeddings...\") --\n  REUSE that backfill path for doc vectors; never re-embed ad hoc.\n- Mining today is SENTENCE-window granularity: _split_phrases +\n  _nphrase_windows(_MAX_NPHRASE=3) yield 1..3-SENTENCE windows;\n  _mine_tag_candidates dedups/downcases them. That is why auto-tag candidates\n  are often whole sentences. Word-level term mining is NEW work. Leave\n  _mine_tag_candidates untouched (doctor's auto-tagger consumes it).\n- There is NO stopword machinery anywhere yet (ef4ad78d deferred \"linguistic\n  pruning\" -- this ticket delivers it for the vocab miner).\n- Everything numeric is pure python (cosine_similarity in todo_embed.py).\n  Keep it that way: NO numpy/umap/hdbscan/nltk deps. Corpus is tens of\n  tickets; O(terms x docs) loops are fine.\n\nDesign decisions (the wisdom -- implementor should not relitigate):\n1. Candidate miner: word-ngram (1..3 words) windows WITHIN _split_phrases\n   boundaries (ngrams never cross a sentence/line break), downcased.\n   Prune: window whose first or last token is a stopword (builtin ~50-word\n   frozenset _STOPWORDS, module-level, no external dep); all-stopword or\n   all-digit windows; tokens < 2 chars; windows > 40 chars. Return\n   {term: set(source ticket Ids)} so provenance rides along.\n2. Doc vector per ticket: mean of its stored Summary/Body chunk vectors,\n   then l2-normalize. One unit vector per ticket Id.\n3. Importance scoring (centroid contrast -- implements \"aligned with doc\n   centroids, far from global corpus centroid\" from the original body):\n     c            = l2-normalized mean of all doc vectors\n     salience(t)  = mean of top-m cos(v_t, d), m = min(3, ndocs)\n     importance(t)= salience(t) - cos(v_t, c)\n   The centroid subtraction IS the first-order hubness correction (a hub\n   term scores high against everything INCLUDING c, so it cancels). This\n   closes ef4ad78d's deferred hubness item. Escalate to CSLS only if hubs\n   demonstrably persist -- not in v1.\n4. Diversity: greedy dedup walking terms by descending importance; drop a\n   term if it is a substring of a kept term (or vice versa) or cos > 0.85\n   to any kept term's vector. Full MMR is overkill.\n5. Persistence: a RECOMPUTABLE CACHE, never part of ticket records.\n   TodoStore.get_vocab(embedder)/put_vocab(embedder, payload); sqlite gets a\n   vocab table, dir backend gets vocab/<embedder>.json under the todo dir.\n   payload = {corpus_fingerprint, computed_at, terms: [{term, score,\n   sources}]} where corpus_fingerprint = sha256 over sorted \"Id:update_dt\"\n   lines. Stale (fingerprint mismatch) or --refresh -> recompute. Deleting\n   the cache must always be harmless.\n6. CLI: `todo terms [-n N] [--embedder=E] [--refresh]` prints global top\n   terms (score, term, #sources); `todo terms <selector>` ranks vocab terms\n   by cosine to that ticket's doc vector (KeyBERT-style). ONE embedder per\n   invocation (error on a comma list -- term scores do not fuse across\n   vector spaces). Default embedder: hash (runs everywhere, CI-safe); docs\n   say \"use --embedder=st for real semantics\". Follow the existing\n   subcommand table pattern (~line 2500 in todo.py).\n7. Empirical guardrail (from the design discussion above): Apple NLCE ranks\n   concept phrases poorly (compressed cosine range, surface-token bias).\n   Do not eyeball-validate the pipeline with apple; use st.\n\nOut of scope for THIS ticket (file follow-ups instead):\n- UMAP/HDBSCAN clustering (drop the cluster column idea; add nothing).\n- Search boost hook (search behavior must not change under anyone's feet).\n- Swapping doctor's auto-tag candidate domain to top-N vocab terms -- that\n  is the eventual payoff, but it changes just-shipped ee1799aa behavior;\n  separate ticket after vocab quality is eyeballed.\n\nTesting strategy (matches the house oracle-test pattern from ee1799aa):\n- Miner: table-driven kept/rejected oracle (e.g. \"semantic tagging\" kept;\n  \"the semantic tagging\" rejected on stopword edge; \"3 5\" rejected).\n- Scoring: hand-built FakeEmbedder in tests with a fixed {text: vector}\n  dict whose geometry PROVES the expected ordering: a cluster-aligned term\n  outranks a hub term near the centroid; near-duplicate terms collapse in\n  dedup. MockEmbedder (sha256) is fine for plumbing but semantically\n  meaningless -- do not assert rankings with it.\n- Persistence: both backends, staleness on fingerprint change.\n- CI never downloads a model: st integration test is skipped when\n  sentence-transformers is absent (same pattern as the apple embedder\n  tests). Full existing suite must stay green -- tag/search behavior is\n  unchanged by this ticket."
  },
